The catalog has only brick components: no chart, text or layout containers. So I built the bar chart as a brick model, with one column per month and column height showing sales. A separate surface holds the title lettering.

<a2ui-json>
[
  {"version":"v0.9.1","createSurface":{"surfaceId":"sales_title","catalogId":"https://a2uicatalog.ai/catalog/blocks-b4.json"}},
  {"version":"v0.9.1","updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"sales_title","components":[
    {"id":"root","component":"motion_bricks","text":"SALES","palette":["#1e66f5","#2f80ed","#56a0f5","#f2994a","#eb5757"],"depth":2,"base":"none","look":"studio","angle":10,"elevation":20,"ratio":"16:9","label":"Sales dashboard title"}
  ]}}
]
</a2ui-json>

<a2ui-json>
[
  {"version":"v0.9.1","createSurface":{"surfaceId":"sales_chart","catalogId":"https://a2uicatalog.ai/catalog/blocks-b4.json"}},
  {"version":"v0.9.1","updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"sales_chart","components":[
    {"id":"root","component":"brick_build_3d","look":"studio","mode":"animate","orbit":true,"height":420,"checks":false,"parts":true,"scrubber":true,"base":"#dfe6ee",
     "bricks":[
       {"x":0,"y":0,"z":0,"w":2,"d":2,"h":3,"c":"#9ec5fe"},
       {"x":3,"y":0,"z":0,"w":2,"d":2,"h":5,"c":"#6ea8fe"},
       {"x":6,"y":0,"z":0,"w":2,"d":2,"h":4,"c":"#3d8bfd"},
       {"x":9,"y":0,"z":0,"w":2,"d":2,"h":7,"c":"#0d6efd"},
       {"x":12,"y":0,"z":0,"w":2,"d":2,"h":6,"c":"#0a58ca"},
       {"x":15,"y":0,"z":0,"w":2,"d":2,"h":9,"c":"#f2994a"}
     ]}
  ]}}
]
</a2ui-json>

The six columns stand for Jan to Jun, with sample values of 3, 5, 4, 7, 6 and 9. June is orange as the peak month. You can drag to orbit the chart, and the scrubber toggles between the build animation and step-by-step instructions. The parts list shows how many bricks the chart uses.
